+# Security Release Notes — binutils (CVE-2025-1180)
+
+## Overview
+
+**CVE-2025-1180** is addressed by the **same upstream fix** as **CVE-2025-11494** (commit b6ac5a8a5b82 in `bfd/elfxx-x86.c`). Ubuntu applied that fix in Noble in **binutils 2.42-4ubuntu2.8** as part of **USN-7919-1** (GNU binutils vulnerabilities, 10 December 2025) when fixing **CVE-2025-11494**. Applying the CVE-2025-1180 code patch on this package yields *"Reversed (or previously applied) patch detected!"* because the fix is already present. This hook only adds this note for compliance; no code patch is applied.
+
+---
+
+## CVE-2025-1180 — x86 .eh_frame / _GLOBAL_OFFSET_TABLE_
+
+- **Component:** binutils, `bfd/elfxx-x86.c`
+- **Issue:** The x86 .eh_frame section may reference `_GLOBAL_OFFSET_TABLE_`. If that symbol is incorrectly removed while the output .eh_frame is non-empty, `_bfd_elf_write_section_eh_frame` can trigger memory corruption.
+- **Fix:** Keep `_GLOBAL_OFFSET_TABLE_` when there is a dynamic section and the output .eh_frame section is non-empty (PR ld/33499).
+
+### Fix lineage (same as CVE-2025-11494)
+
+| Attribute | Value |
+|-----------|--------|
+| **Upstream commit** | b6ac5a8a5b82f0ae6a5642c8d7149b325f4cc60a |
+| **Bug** | https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=32642 |
+| **Already applied in Noble as** | CVE-2025-11494 fix in 2.42-4ubuntu2.8 (USN-7919-1) |
+
+**Verification:** The fix is present in 2.42-4ubuntu2.8. Applying the upstream patch reports "Reversed (or previously applied) patch detected! Skipping patch."
+
+### Recommendation
+
+- Treat **CVE-2025-1180** as **already remediated** for binutils 2.42-4ubuntu2.8 (Noble) via the CVE-2025-11494 fix. No additional patch required.
